  "body": "Hello.\n\nThanks for the amazing work you did with ART. I use it for many years now, and I'm really happy.\n\nI've got a series of RAW files (Canon CR3) with which I got a strange behaviour.\nI do all my work, and the preview in ART is ok.\nBut when added to the process list, and exported in JPG, all pictures are bugged.\nIt seems the color balance is not the same between the preview and the exported version.\nI was using last version 1.25.2. But I've got the same behaviour with the last 1.24 version.\n\nThis happens with the \"auto\" color balance.\nNote that sometimes (not for all the serie), the sliders are not the usual sliders.\nIt's red / green / blue sliders, instead of temperature and color dominance.\n\nDon't hesitate to ask for more informations if needed.\nHere are the different files : \n\n![ART interface with preview](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5373def8-2aee-49f9-8cfa-4dc480cf30ea)\n\n![Exported version](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b72a234a-1b10-4a91-aa84-34fe0238a1f2)\n\nHere's a link to all files (CR3, ARP, camera jpg file, exported jpg file) : https://limewire.com/d/cc2e2ea3-9ba5-44fa-9492-2b373c74403c#b8j8kwX-uOLx7z86gzPWUeSz96AtuVbr-JsiubwdJDk\n\nSorry, it seems I can't put it directly on github.\n\n\nMichaël",
